    "D": "common delay parameter d",
    "N": "number of agents"
   },
   "conditions": [
    "G connected undirected"
   ],
   "tuning": [
    "individual learning rates gamma(v) set by a local doubling trick"
   ],
   "is_new": true,
   "source": {
    "label": "th:main",
    "number": "Theorem (th:main)",
    "quote": "The regret of {\\sc Exp3-Coop} run over a network $G = (V,E)$ of $N$ agents, each using delay $d$, and an individual learning rate $\\eta(v) = \\gamma(v)/\\bigl(Ke(d+1)\\bigr)$, where $\\gamma(v) \\in (0,1]$ is adaptively selected by each agent through the above doubling trick, satisfies, when $T$ grows large, R_T^{coop} = O(sqrt((ln K)(d+1+K/N alpha(G_{<=d}))T) + d log T)."
   },
   "confidence": "high",
   "notes": "Remark: with d = sqrt(K), for any connected G this gives K^{1/4} sqrt(T ln K) + sqrt(K) ln T."
  },
